# Critical: .dart_tool/package_config.json records ABSOLUTE host paths into
# the host's pub-cache (e.g. /home/<user>/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/...).
# The Dockerfile runs `flutter pub get` *inside* the container (producing a
# container-correct package_config.json pointing at the container's own
# pub-cache), then `COPY . .` -- without this file, that COPY overwrites the
# container-correct .dart_tool/ with the host's stale, host-path one, and
# every plugin then fails to compile ("package com.ryanheise.just_audio
# does not exist", etc. for every plugin) because those host paths don't
# exist inside the container. Found by actually running `make mobile-apk`.
.dart_tool/
build/
build-output/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Also host-specific / regenerated by the container's own tooling.
android/.gradle/
android/app/.cxx/
android/local.properties
.idea/
*.iml
android/*.iml

.git/
.gitignore
